-- Markup nested more deeply than the checker follows is one
-- `nesting_too_deep`, worded for markup, at the innermost hole the checker
-- reached (14:8405), and nothing more: the part it could not read is poisoned,
-- so no hole reports that it cannot tell its type. 1 400 levels of
-- `<div>{…}</div>` is the fewest the checker gives up on while the parser
-- accepts them. The message is about markup, not a type and a type alias,
-- and no second message, a `child_not_renderable`, says a hole's type is
-- unknown.
import Html exposing (Html)


